To upload a file when the input element is created dynamically, you can handle the `filechooser` event or use a waiting method upon your action.

### Recommended Approach: Using `page.waitForEvent`
You should start waiting for the file chooser before performing the action that triggers it (such as clicking a button). This ensures you capture the event correctly.

```javascript
// Start waiting for file chooser before clicking. Note no await.
const fileChooserPromise = page.waitForEvent('filechooser');
await page.getByLabel('Upload file').click();
const fileChooser = await fileChooserPromise;
await fileChooser.setFiles(path.join(__dirname, 'myfile.pdf'));
```

### Alternative Approach: Using `page.on('filechooser')`
You can also handle the event using a listener. This is triggered when the file chooser appears:

```javascript
page.on('filechooser', async fileChooser => {
  await fileChooser.setFiles(path.join(__dirname, '/tmp/myfile.pdf'));
});
```

Both methods utilize `fileChooser.setFiles()` to upload the file once the chooser is available.

